  <note>
    <content textType="body">
      <p>The whole public surface is two endpoints. POST /payments takes the card data and returns the outcome; GET /payment/{id} lets the merchant look a past payment back up. A subtle design point: Authorized and Declined both come back as 201 - HTTP success means we processed the request, and the business answer is a field in the body. Only Rejected, where we refuse to even try, is a 400. The full contract is generated into Swagger UI from the controller annotations, so the documentation cannot drift from the code.</p>
    </content>
  </note>
